As electropositive character increases down the group, the basic character of the oxide increases. For Group 13 elements, the trend in basicity of their oxides is:
\underbrace{B_{2}O_{3}}_{\text{acidic}} \lt \underbrace{Al_{2}O_{3} \lt Ga_{2}O_{3}}_{\text{amphoteric}} \lt \underbrace{In_{2}O_{3} \lt Tl_{2}O_{3}}_{\text{basic}}
Therefore, \(Tl_{2}O_{3}\) is the most basic oxide among the given options.

### For option (A):

2B + 2NH_{3} \rightarrow 2BN + 3H_{2}
Boron produced BN with ammonia but \textbf{Boron} is element not compound. So that this option not involve in answer.

### For option (B):

3B_{2}H_{6} + 6NH_{3} \xrightarrow{T=200^{\circ}C} 3[BH_{2}(NH_{3})_{2}]^{+}[BH_{4}^{-}] \rightarrow 2B_{3}N_{3}H_{6} + 12H_{2}
B_{3}N_{3}H_{6} \xrightarrow{T>200^{\circ}C} (BN)_{x}

### For option (C):

B_{2}O_{3}(\ell) + 2NH_{3} \xrightarrow{1200^{\circ}C} 2BN_{(s)} + 3H_{2}O_{(g)}

### For option (D):

HBF_{4} + NH_{3} \rightarrow NH_{4}[BF_{4}]
